{%- doc -%}
  The colour picker, the price and the add to cart button, in one form.

  Split out of wf-product so that section fits inside the Admin API's 16,384
  character limit for one GraphQL document. Nothing else changed.

  @param {object} product - the product being bought
  @param {object} settings - the section settings, for the labels
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The picker and the buy box share one form, which is the whole trick.

  Each swatch is a radio named "id" carrying a variant id, so the
  selected radio *is* the value the cart receives. No script computes
  it, no hidden field has to be kept in step, and the form posts the
  right variant with JavaScript switched off. The hidden input survives
  only for a product that has no options to choose between.

  A variant with a picture gets the picture. One without gets its name
  in a pill, so the row is useful the day the options are created and
  upgrades by itself the day the photographs are assigned, with nothing
  here to change in between.

  Sold-out variants stay in the row, disabled and struck through,
  because a colour that silently disappears reads as a page that is
  broken rather than as a colour that is gone.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- form 'product', product, class: 'wf-pdp__form' -%}
  {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
    <fieldset class="wf-sw">
      <legend class="wf-sw__legend">{{ settings.swatch_label }}</legend>
      <div class="wf-sw__row">
        {%- for v in product.variants -%}
          {%- assign checked = false -%}
          {%- if v.id == product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id -%}
            {%- assign checked = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <label class="wf-sw__i{% unless v.available %} wf-sw__i--out{% endunless %}">
            <input
              class="wf-sw__in"
              type="radio"
              name="id"
              value="{{ v.id }}"
              {% if checked %}checked{% endif %}
              {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
            >
            {%- if v.image -%}
              <img
                class="wf-sw__img"
                src="{{ v.image | image_url: width: 220 }}"
                width="88"
                height="88"
                alt=""
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              >
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="wf-sw__t">{{ v.title }}</span>
          </label>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </fieldset>
  {%- endunless -%}

  <div class="wf-buybox">
    <p class="wf-pdp__price">
      {{ product.price | money }}
      {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
        <s class="wf-pdp__was">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      Unconditional, because the rate behind it is. Shipping is free on
      every order in the Israel zone at any cart total, so this line is
      not a claim about this product clearing a threshold, it is a fact
      about the shop. It sits inside the buy box rather than above it,
      so it is read in the same glance as the price.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.price_note != blank -%}
      <p class="wf-pdp__ship">{{ settings.price_note }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if product.has_only_default_variant -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
    {%- endif -%}
    <button type="submit" class="wf-btn wf-pdp__submit" {% unless product.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
      {%- if product.available -%}{{ settings.atc_label }}{%- else -%}אזל מהמלאי{%- endif -%}
    </button>

    {%- if settings.note != blank -%}
      <p class="wf-pdp__note">{{ settings.note }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endform -%}

